   "spoken": "When Black defends e6 but allows the queen to h5, don't rush the tempting knight to f7 — a queen retreat to e8 would pin it. The Russian-school choice is to drop the knight back modestly: his king is wretched, so there's no need to force a win amid the complications. Then complete development — the knight reroutes to d4 exploiting the pin and blockading his passer, the bishop to f4 sets up an x-ray at the king, and the pawn levers b4 and a4 tear open the c- and a-files, where discovered-attack and mating ideas do the rest.",
